12. Scope: Separation of Concerns

12.1 What UMIR is not

· It is not a notation system.
· It is not a protocol.
· It is not an educational method.
· It is not a universal musical ontology.

12.2 The educational claim is separate

V0.2's Phase 6 (educational experiment) and FC5 (kernel-first inferior to existing methods) conflated two research programs. Education is a separate empirical question, addressed in a separate paper. The UMIR project does not die if kernel-first is pedagogically inferior.

12.3 The planetary claim

The "planetary-agnostic" framing is architectural, not empirical. UMIR does not claim to be independent of physiology or acoustics. It claims that structural representation can be agnostic to planetary parameters, which are supplied by the renderer.

