Appendix C — Kernel Algebra Formal Specification

C.1 Grammar

```
kernel    ::= ⟨ events, fields, gtree, gcycle, gdep, constraints, metadata ⟩

events    ::= { event* }
event     ::= ( time, pitch, duration, amplitude, timbre, articulation )

fields    ::= { field* }
field     ::= ( interval, function )

gtree     ::= ( nodes, edges, root )
nodes     ::= { node* }
node      ::= ( id, content )

gcycle    ::= { cycle* }
cycle     ::= ( period, phase, content, count )

gdep      ::= { dep* }
dep       ::= ( source, target, relation )

constraints ::= { constraint* }
constraint ::= predicate

metadata  ::= { key : value* }
```

C.2 Well-Formedness Conditions

W1. Every event time t \in [0, H] for the declared horizon H.

W2. Every duration d > 0.

W3. Every field function is defined on its declared interval.

W4. G_{\text{tree}} is a rooted tree: every node except the root has exactly one parent; the root has none; no cycles.

W5. G_{\text{dep}} is a DAG: no directed cycles.

W6. Every cycle period p > 0; every phase \phi \in [0, p).

W7. Every constraint references only components present in the kernel.

W8. Every metadata key is either a defined kernel key or a namespaced extension key.

C.3 Composition Operations

Concatenation. For k_1, k_2 \in \mathcal{K}:

k_1 \otimes k_2 = \langle E_1 \cup E_2', F_1 \cup F_2', \ldots \rangle

where primes indicate time-shifting of k_2 by the horizon of k_1.

Parallel composition. For k_1, k_2 \in \mathcal{K}:

k_1 \parallel k_2 = \langle E_1 \cup E_2, F_1 \cup F_2, \ldots \rangle

with dependencies added to record simultaneity.

Repetition. For k \in \mathcal{K} and n \in \mathbb{N}:

k^{\times n} = k \otimes k \otimes \cdots \otimes k \quad (n \text{ times})

Cycle wrapping. For k \in \mathcal{K} and period p:

\text{cycle}(k, p) = \langle \varnothing, \varnothing, \varnothing, \{(p, 0, k, \infty)\}, \varnothing, \varnothing, \varnothing \rangle

